<title>HUNGARY: CESI index eases drops ahead of weekend.</title>
<headline>CESI index eases drops ahead of weekend.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index dropped on Friday to close at 1,508.77 points, down 4.87 points or 0.32 percent, the Budapest Stock Stock Exchange said. The index's fall was triggered by losses on the Polish and the Czech market.</p>
<p>The index, which has been published since February 1, reflects trends of 50 shares on the Budapest, Prague and Warsaw bourses.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410</p>
